<title>Algorithm for Screening and Diagnosis of Phenylketonuria in Newborns.</title>
<graphic href="eee0084-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Newborn screening test</label>
<path target="cell-2">Negative</path>
<path target="cell-3">Positive</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Infant older than 24 h when test performed?</label>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Rescreen</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>PKU unlikely</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Measure serum phenylalanine</label>
<path target="cell-5">Under 4 mg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-6">4–10 mg/dL</path>
<path target="cell-7">Over 10 mg/dL</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Hyperphenylalaninemia</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>PKU. Consider confirmatory DNA probe for phenylalanine hydroxylase gene. Begin low-phenylalanine diet</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>*These cutoff values may vary by state or lab corporation.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
